 [:a {:href "/athletes/9827"} "Walter Hofmann"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/9807"} "Rolf-Dieter Amend"] " of East Germany, the reigning World runners-up in the C-2 and champions in the C-2 team with Kretschmer and Trummer. Their counterparts in the West held the number two position with " [:a {:href "/athletes/9978"} "Hans-Otto Schumacher"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/9888"} "Willi Baues"] ". Neither East German team improved upon their record in the second run, which was enough for Hofmann and Amend to earn gold, but France bettered its time sufficiently to leapfrog ahead of Schumacher and Baues. The West Germans, however, performed even better in run two and maintained their silver medal position, leaving France with bronze and Kretschmer and Trummer, who failed to post a score, off the podium."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Bib"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Total Time"] [:th {} "Run #1"] [:th {} "Run #2"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "139/124"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/9827"} "Walter Hofmann"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/9807"} "Rolf-Dieter Amend"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GDR.png"}] "GDR"]] [:td {} "310.68"] [:td {} "310.68 (1)"] [:td {} "445.51 (10)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "190/158"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/9978"} "Hans-Otto Schumacher"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/9888"} "Willi Baues"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRG"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRG.png"}] "FRG"]] [:td {} "311.90"] [:td {} "316.96 (2)"] [:td {} "311.90 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {